From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:03:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] avutil/hwcontext_v4l2request: read the OUTPUT capabilities of
 the codec format

A driver may hold a CAPTURE buffer for one codec and not another, as
Hantro does for H.264 alone: the capabilities read before the codec's
format is set are the default format's. Read them again once it is set,
so a decoder that takes a picture whole is handed one.
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
index c885c68..817e387 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
@@ -594,6 +594,15 @@ static int v4l2request_probe_video_device(AVHWFramesContext *hwfc,
         goto fail;
     }
 
+    // The capabilities again, now of the codec format: holding a CAPTURE buffer may depend on it
+    buffers = (struct v4l2_create_buffers) {
+        .count = 0,
+        .memory = V4L2_MEMORY_MMAP,
+        .format.type = fctxi->output.format.type,
+    };
+    if (ioctl(fctxi->video_fd, VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS, &buffers) >= 0)
+        fctxi->output.capabilities = buffers.capabilities;
+
     /*
      * Set any codec specific controls that can help assist the driver
      * make a decision on what CAPTURE buffer format can be used.
